--- !u!114 &7859591419096915612
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2066512746159596452}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e2e0107d76b6e4643a068d9c2384e0d7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Lalim.UI.LoadingScreen
  _progressBar: {fileID: 2687676132020358214}
  _progressText: {fileID: 6302963966232663844}
  _tipText: {fileID: 574846085352926685}
  _categoryText: {fileID: 9056799636382629984}
  _factGroup: {fileID: 1153923789751525796}
  _statusText: {fileID: 0}
  _regionArtwork: {fileID: 0}
  _facts:
  - category: Deity
    text: "Amansinaya is the Tagalog patron of fishermen. Before casting their nets,
      fisherfolk whistled to her and said \"Kasump\xE2 ak\xF3\": I am your sworn
      friend."
  - category: Deity
    text: Fisherfolk never ate their first catch. They gave it back to Amansinaya,
      so the sea would give again.
  - category: Deity
    text: Haik is a Tagalog sea spirit that sailors called on for protection from
      storms at sea.
  - category: Deity
    text: Neguno, the sagacious ruler of the sea, turned the greedy boat owner Kablay
      into the very first shark.
  - category: Relic
    text: 'The Radiant Conch: fisherfolk blew conches across the water to call one
      another home. Amansinaya gives it to whoever heals her shallows.'
  - category: Relic
    text: Haik's Compass guided every sailor who called his name, and it never once
      lied about the way home.
  - category: Relic
    text: The Woven Net Fragment was woven by honest hands, made to take only what
      is needed and let the rest swim free.
  - category: Relic
    text: Relics you earn from Luzon's deities will be needed in the waters of the
      Visayas.
  - category: Tool
    text: The Water Sampling Kit reads the water's pH, salinity and temperature.
      Healthy reef water sits between pH 7.9 and 8.4.
  - category: Tool
    text: "Healthy reef water holds 33 to 37 parts per thousand of salt, and stays
      between 24 and 29 \xB0C."
  - category: Tool
    text: Coral Seeds only take root on clean rock. Clear the dead ground before
      you plant.
  - category: Tool
    text: Sort trash into plastic, glass and metal. What is sorted properly can be
      made new again.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Spirit Sense makes hidden things glow, and a spirit wisp leads you to whatever
      you need next.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Tap Surge for a quick dash. You can chain up to three in a row.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: "Hold the Surge button to ride a Riptide: 1.75\xD7 swim speed for a whole
      minute."
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Call your dugong with Tidebond and ride it to cross open water faster.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Your health never comes back on its own. Seagrass Mend heals you over three
      seconds.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Bubble Barrier charges while you swim and use other skills. While it's
      up, toxic water can't hurt you.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Your dugong has its own health. Keep it out of toxic water, or shelter
      it inside your Bubble Barrier.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Polluted water slowly drains your health, but talking with the deities
      and playing minigames pauses it.
  - category: Mechanic
    text: Respawning at a checkpoint restores your health and stamina, so one bad
      run never follows you.
  - category: Ocean fact
    text: Dugongs are the only plant-eating mammals that live entirely in the sea.
      They graze on seagrass meadows.
  - category: Ocean fact
    text: Ghost nets are fishing nets lost or abandoned at sea. They keep trapping
      animals for years.
  - category: Ocean fact
    text: The Philippines lies in the Coral Triangle, home to more kinds of coral
      and reef fish than anywhere else on Earth.
  - category: Ocean fact
    text: When water gets too warm, coral spits out the tiny algae that feed it,
      turns white, and starts to starve. This is called bleaching.
  - category: Tip
    text: Lost? The quest box in the top-left corner always shows what to do next.
      Tap the key to open or close it.
  - category: Tip
    text: Talk to the statues. Each deity has a task, and a gift for whoever completes
      it.
  - category: Tip
    text: Trash can hide behind coral and rocks. Use Spirit Sense to make every piece
      glow.
  _factSeconds: 7
  _factFadeSeconds: 0.35
  _baseLoadingText: Loading
  _statusCycleInterval: 0.4
  _barSmoothSpeed: 5
